{"term":"sort out","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:dda6ab4876db2d8875","definition":"To clarify by reviewing mentally.","example":"It's a bit confused at the moment, I'll try to sort it out later.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["sort oneself out"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort_out#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0fa0361f85d407fd5f","definition":"To arrange.","example":"Could you call Dave and sort out a meeting for tomorrow?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["sort oneself out"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort_out#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fb59f006899e609cfd","definition":"To fix (a problem).","example":"The computer won't let me delete that file; could you sort it out?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["sort oneself out"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort_out#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:055b2a970568aab0a9","definition":"To organise or separate into groups, as a collection of items, so as to make tidy.","example":"Could you sort out your wardrobe and put the clothes you no longer use in one pile to give away and another to throw away?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["sort oneself out"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort_out#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:83513cd3e2244e7